        "id": "military-art/H-003-1 Asheville's Defiance.jpg",
        "src": "content/artwork/curated/military-art/H-003-1%20Asheville's%20Defiance.jpg",
        "caption": "USS Asheville (PG-21) — the first Navy ship named for the city, commissioned in 1920. After years showing the flag from Central America to China, she retreated toward Australia as the Philippines fell, and was sunk south of Java on March 3, 1942, by a Japanese cruiser and two destroyers — nearly her entire crew lost."
      },
      {
