        "src": "content/artwork/curated/military-art/USS_Asheville_(PG-84)_underway_in_1966.jpg",
        "caption": "USS Asheville (PG-84) — a Ashville-class patrol gunboat commissioned in 1966 and deployed to Vietnam's coastal waters under Operation Market Time, intercepting enemy supply traffic; the second Navy ship to carry the city's name."
      },
